course: dictionary
lesson: 10669
title: Unlucky, and what it really means
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unlucky means having bad luck, when things go wrong by chance. «Ollie is unlucky, not cheated, unless the game promised a guarantee.» Both words are about a game going badly, but they are different. Unlucky means the dice or cards just went against him. Cheated means someone did something wrong on purpose.
explain: The word can also be a kind thing to say. When someone just misses, you say «unlucky!» to show you feel sorry for them. The same word can mean a kind comfort or a fact about chance, so look at the sentence to see which one it is.
explain: Some people believe certain things bring bad luck, like the number 13, black cats or broken mirrors. Stories also call owls unlucky: «Stories call owls wise, unlucky or ill when they fly by day, but the real owl is simply a superb hunter.» These are beliefs, not facts. Ask yourself: is this a fact, or a story people tell?
fact: Unlucky means having bad luck, when things go wrong by chance.
fact: Unlucky can describe a person, a thing or a number: «an unlucky number».
fact: Unlucky can mean sad that something did not happen: «you were unlucky not to win».
fact: Some people believe 13, black cats and broken mirrors are unlucky, but these are only superstitions, not facts.
fact: The adverb is unluckily. Unluckier and unluckiest compare how much bad luck there is.
exercise: «Ollie is unlucky, not cheated, unless the game promised a guarantee.» What does unlucky mean here? | Won a prize for playing well | *Bad luck, when things go wrong by chance | Cheated by the other players | Ran very fast
exercise: Some people believe a black cat is unlucky. What is this? | A rule of the game | *A belief, not a fact, called a superstition | A kind of bird | A scientific fact proven in a laboratory
exercise: Dad says «unlucky!» when you miss the goal by an inch. What does he mean? | He wants you to pass the ball | *He feels sorry, because you nearly got it | He thinks the goal was too big | He is angry that you lost
test: «You were unlucky not to win.» What does this sentence mean? | You did not want to play at all | *You missed winning, and the speaker feels sorry for you | You were the loudest player | You won the prize
test: Which word is the adverb of unlucky? | Luck | Luckily | Unluckier | *Unluckily
exam: Are black cats unlucky? Choose the best answer. | Yes, but only on Tuesdays | *It is only a superstition, a belief some people have | Yes, they always bring bad luck, it is a proven fact | Black cats are never seen at night
